Create Employee Onboarding and Training Manuals
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Structure a multi-section employee onboarding guide using Markdown
Write clear, step-by-step technical instructions with visual aid placeholders
Build a standalone training manual with learning objectives, exercises, and a knowledge-check quiz
Apply accessibility best practices (alt-text, heading hierarchy, font readability)
Compile multiple Markdown documents into a single branded PDF documentation package
Prerequisites
Basic familiarity with Markdown syntax (headings, lists, links, images)
Comfortable using a Linux terminal (navigating directories, editing files)
No prior PDF tooling experience required — instructions provided
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Linux machine via Start Lab. Run the following to prepare your workspace and tools.

# Update package index and install required tools
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y pandoc texlive-latex-base texlive-fonts-recommended imagemagick nano

# Create project directory structure
mkdir -p ~/onboarding-project/{docs,images,output}
cd ~/onboarding-project
Verify installation:

pandoc --version
